# What a render makes in here, on top of the shared list at the repository root.
# The root already carries *_silent.mp4, *_pops.wav, *_cues.txt and *_sheet.png;
# these two are Micro's own and are outputs in the same sense.
#
# The riser is impact.finale's chord at the engine's own level, written to its
# own file since 8 September so that POP_GAIN never touches it - one command
# remakes it. The finale instant comes out of flowanim.py the way the badge cues
# do, and an output kept in history is an output somebody eventually edits.
*_riser.wav
*_finale.txt

# preview_bed_*.mp4 and proba_*.mp4 are auditions - a bed or a level being
# compared under a finished clip - and are covered by the root's *.mp4 already.
# Named here so nobody adds them back deliberately.
preview_*.mp4
proba_*.mp4

# make_fixture.py's output. Derived, deterministically, from an Organs poster
# and the anchored base - which is the test this repository applies everywhere:
# a poster is tracked because no command can remake it, and a fixture is not,
# because one can. `./make_fixture.py ../../Organs/work/<topic>_poster.jpeg demo`
# rebuilds it and prints what is left around each right circle.
*_fixture.png
